highOrderManufacturedFDAImplicitPETScDistributed.C

/* Added for cardiacFoam: this is a working copy of
   highOrderManufacturedFDAImplicitPETScParallel, taken once the LRE ->
   movingLeastSquares port was verified against the serial reference (10
   configurations, convergence orders within 0.021).

   That sibling keeps the verified state: it uses the parallel high-order
   library but still assembles a single Eigen sparse matrix and hands the
   finished CSR to PETSc purely as a linear solver, which is serial by
   construction.

   This copy is where the linear algebra becomes genuinely distributed. Keeping
   the two side by side means the algebra change can be compared against a
   known-good baseline instead of against the memory of one. */
EXE = $(FOAM_USER_APPBIN)/highOrderManufacturedFDAImplicitPETScDistributed
